# Cowork Scheduled Task 6: Weekly SEO Report

> **⚠ PYTHONPATH REQUIRED (fix 2026-07-16).** Every `python3 scripts/...` call in this task MUST be run as `cd ~/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup && PYTHONPATH=.pip-packages python3 scripts/...`. The google-api libraries live in `.pip-packages/`; without PYTHONPATH the run fails with "google-auth not installed" or misreports the OAuth token as expired (this caused the false "GSC credentials expired" outage 07-14→07-16 — the token was healthy the whole time; verified + refreshed 2026-07-16). If a refresh ever genuinely fails with invalid_grant, retry once 60s later before declaring the credential dead, and include the exact exception text in the log.

# Cadence: Every Monday at 11:00 AM
# Working folder: ~/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/

---

You are generating the weekly SEO performance report for Mindtalk (mindtalk.in).

## Your job

Run the weekly report scripts and produce four files:
1. Summary CSV — site-level WoW (matches historical format)
2. Queries CSV — every query with WoW deltas
3. Clusters CSV — category and topic cluster level tracking
4. Markdown report — full readable summary

## Steps

### Step 1 — Run the weekly report script
```
python3 ~/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/scripts/weekly-report.py
```

### Step 2 — Run the cluster report script
```
python3 ~/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/scripts/cluster-report.py
```

### Step 3 — Read both reports
Read:
- ~/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/reports/weekly-report-[TODAY].md
- ~/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/reports/clusters-[TODAY].csv

### Step 4 — Write plain-English summary
Write to ~/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/reports/weekly-summary-[TODAY].txt covering:
- Overall traffic direction (up/down/stable) with numbers
- Best performing category this week by impressions
- Category with biggest WoW improvement
- Top rising topic cluster (e.g. "Depression queries improved X positions on average")
- Top dropping topic cluster if any
- Top 3 queries by impressions
- Any rank drops flagged for content refresh
- One key action item for the SEO team this week

### Step 4.5 — GA4 channel mix (added 2026-07-10 — Supermetrics MCP)

Pull the weekly channel table from GA4 via the Supermetrics MCP (source `GAWA`, property `395357273`): fields `sessionDefaultChannelGrouping, sessions, engagedSessions, conversions`, `date_range_type=last_7_days`, timezone Asia/Kolkata (data_query → get_async_query_results). Add to the summary:
- Organic Search sessions + conversions WoW (GA4's independent read alongside GSC clicks — flag if they diverge >25%, that's a tracking or brand-SERP issue)
- **AI Assistant channel** sessions WoW (native GA4 channel — the P5 AI-search KPI)
- Paid Search sessions (context only — notes paid/organic interplay while ads are running)

If Supermetrics is unavailable, log `GA4 SKIPPED` and continue — never block the report on it.

### Step 5 — Flag drops for refresh
Review dropping queries and clusters. If any keyword dropped 5+ positions:
- Add to ~/Seo-workflow-mindtalk/mindtalk-setup/flagged-drops.json so Task 2 picks it up

## Step 6 — Post to Slack

Post a summary to **#seo-workflow-mindtalk** (channel ID: `C0AUAPS4J83`) using `slack_send_message`.

Format:

```
📊 *Weekly SEO Report — [WEEK START] to [WEEK END]*
Site: mindtalk.in

*Traffic:*
> Clicks: [N] ([+/-N%] WoW)
> Impressions: [N] ([+/-N%] WoW)
> CTR: [N%] | Avg Position: [N]

*Top Category:* [category] — [impressions] impressions
*Best Improving Cluster:* [cluster name] — [+N%] impressions WoW
*Worst Dropping Cluster:* [cluster name] — [N%] impressions WoW

*Top 3 Queries by Impressions:*
> 1. [query] — [impressions] impr, pos [N]
> 2. [query] — [impressions] impr, pos [N]
> 3. [query] — [impressions] impr, pos [N]

*Rising:* [N] queries | *Dropping:* [N] queries | *New:* [N] queries

[If any queries flagged for refresh:]
⚠️ [N] queries flagged for content refresh review

📎 Full report: reports/weekly-report-[DATE].md
```

## Output

Tell me:
- Clicks and impressions this week with WoW change
- Top performing category
- Best improving cluster
- Worst dropping cluster (if any)
- Files created
